Q: Why is my JavaScript fetch request not returning JSON data correctly? A: <p>with not much data available we would like to see the data from the server that you get. In chrome you can press f12 and go to the tab network. if you refresh your page or redo the api call you can see the error there if it happens.</p>
<pre><code>fetch(&quot;https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1&quot;)
  .then(response =&gt; {
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP error! Status: ${response.status}`);
    }
    return response.json();
  })
  .then(data =&gt; {
    console.log(data);
  })
  .catch(error =&gt; {
    console.error(&quot;Error:&quot;, error);
  });
</code></pre>

Q: RabbitMQ consumer not called in ASP.NET Core A: <p>The problem is the lifetime of your connection and channel.</p>
<p>In your method you have:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using var connection = await factory.CreateConnectionAsync();
using var channel = await connection.CreateChannelAsync();
</code></pre>
<p>When <code>AddConsumer()</code> finishes executing, the method returns and the using blocks dispose the connection and channel. That stops the consumer immediately.</p>
<p>When you restart the app, the method runs again, briefly creates the consumer, processes queued messages, then disposes again.</p>
<p>To resolve that, you'd need to store <code>connection</code> and <code>channel</code> in fields, for instance:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class RMQConfig
{
    private IConnection? _connection;
    private IChannel? _channel;

    public async Task AddConsumer()
    {
        var factory = new ConnectionFactory { HostName = &quot;localhost&quot; };

        _connection = await factory.CreateConnectionAsync();
        _channel = await _connection.CreateChannelAsync();

        // ...
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>You'd need probably to implement <code>IDisposable</code> to correctly dispose of <code>connection</code> and <code>channel</code>, and then register <code>RMQConfig</code> as singleton.</p>
